    "title": "Escape the Spreading Fire",
    "category": "Queue",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "You are given an m \u00d7 n grid containing: 0 for empty land 1 for fire 2 for walls You start at the top-left cell and want to reach the bottom-right cell. Each minute: You may move to an adjacent empty cell. Fire simultaneously spreads to adjacent non-wall cells. Determine the maximum number of minutes you can wait before starting your journey while still being able to safely reach the destination. Return -1 if reaching the destination is impossible.",
    "input": "Integers m and n An m \u00d7 n grid",
    "output": "A single integer.",
    "constraints": "1 <= m, n <= 300"
